<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western Jin dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Western Jin dynasty was a Chinese dynasty that ruled from 265 to 316 CE, founded by the Sima family, which seized power from the Wei state. It briefly reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 280 CE, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> profile places it in the aftermath of Han collapse, and it soon fell into civil war and to invasions by northern peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-jin-dynasty.jpg" alt="Western Jin dynasty" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ian Kiu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Jeun_Dynasty_280_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
